  "ai_show_review": {
    "summary": "Tight jams, stellar China>Rider and explosive The Other One > Mind Left Body",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a soaring second set with a ferocious The Other One → Mind Left Body excursion and a classic China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue. Jerry’s guitar is on fire while Phil lays down bomb‑like bass, and Keith’s piano sits forward in the mix. Highlights include Weather Report Suite, To Lay Me Down and a soulful set of ballads.",
    "review": "Denver Coliseum on November 20, 1973 captured one of the fall tour’s high points. The first set rolls through tight country‑rock numbers – Brown‑Eyed Women, Beat It On Down The Line, To Lay Me Down and a beautifully executed Weather Report Suite (Prelude → Part 1 → Let It Grow) that sets up a confident Casey Jones finale. The second set is where the magic truly ignites: a thunderous Mississippi Half‑Step into Dire Wolf leads straight into a blistering Promised Land → Bertha → Greatest Story Ever Told medley, then the band launches into an inspired China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition. From there, Truckin’ erupts into a bass‑bombed The Other One that seamlessly morphs into an expansive Mind Left Body jam, before winding down with a haunting Stella Blue and a sweet Sugar Magnolia. Throughout, Jerry’s tone is crystal‑clear and “peaking,” Phil’s bass is described as “bombs away,” and Keith’s piano shines unusually forward in the mix – a rare treat for 1973 recordings. The encore’s Uncle John’s Band rounds out an evening that feels both tight and exploratory, making this show a must‑listen for any Deadhead seeking classic ’73 chemistry.",
